---
import LetsTalk from '@components/home/LetsTalk.astro'
import Insight from '@components/insights/Insight.astro'
import InsightSignoff from '@components/insights/InsightSignoff.astro'
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
import { getInsightNav } from '@data/insights'
import InsightNav from '@components/insights/InsightNav.astro'

const { previous, current, next } = getInsightNav('what-about-off-shoring')
---

<Layout title={current?.title} description={current?.summary}>
  <Insight>
    <span slot="insight-title">{current?.title}</span>
    <span slot="insight-subtitle">{current?.dateLabel}</span>
    <span slot="insight-text">
      <p>
        You're probably expecting us to say that off-shoring is a bad idea, you should never do it, it's scary, etc. And
        we should, as it is direct competition to our services. But the truth is, off-shoring can be a good idea in some
        circumstances. That's why all the big four banks have been doing it for years. It's not inherently bad, it just
        has to be managed well.
      </p><br />
      <p>
        If you have the below skills/capabilities in-house, then off-shoring can be a good way to save money on
        development costs:
        <ul class="lg:mt-4">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
            Time and ability to work with a team in a different timezone
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
            Understanding of cultural differences and communication styles
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>Strong project management skills
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>Ability to clearly define requirements and
            expectations
          </li>
        </ul>
      </p><br />

      <p>
        If you think you have the above capabilities and are prepared to manage the risks, then here are some tips for
        you to help you succeed:
        <ul class="lg:mt-4">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
            Write your requirements in User Stories format and include acceptance criteria for each story. This will help
            ensure that everyone has a clear understanding of what needs to be built and how it will be tested.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>
            Ensure you have access to the source code from day one. Download a copy of the codebase if not each day, then
            each week at minimum.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>Have the off-shore team provide you with the
            technical documentation before starting the project. Have this reviewed by someone technical.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>You'll generally have better results if you have the
            design done locally and provide it to the off-shore team.
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3 ml-2 lg:ml-4 lg:my-1">
            <span
              class="shrink-0 w-[12px] h-[12px] mt-[2.5px] lg:mt-[5px]"
              style={`background-color: var(--accent-bgc);`}></span>Ensure you have a contract in place that includes
            clear deliverables, timelines, and payment terms.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </p><br />

      <p>
        If you don't have those capabilities, or you need help managing the risks, then we can help consult so that you
        are in a better position to succeed.
      </p><br />
      <InsightSignoff />
    </span>
  </Insight>
  <InsightNav previousInsight={previous} nextInsight={next} />

  <LetsTalk />
</Layout>
